#  OneOS package set x9u-in-1105-a16 (testers only, 0.5.51): sha256sum of out/overlays_x9u_in_1105_a16_r7, ColorOS 17 (Find X9 Ultra IN 1105) on Android 16 / One UI 8 phones (Galaxy S22 series), minus tethering_payload.img OneOSWallpapersFoldGrid.apk. r1: x9u_in_1105_r11's files without the One UI 9.5 camera files; services, framework and telephony-common with switcher/patches/a16_connectivity_compat.py (ONEOS_A16CC_ABSENT_OK=1); framework_patched_oneui8.jar and framework_patched_oneui85.jar (switcher/patches/a16_camera.py); the image's conscrypt profiling os.statsd media media.swcodec resolv ipsec uwb devicelock scheduling neuralnetworks tzdata uprobestats payloads and tethering_connectivity_native_a17.so, 2026-11-26. r2: nfcservices_payload.img and npumanager_payload.img (oneui95_a16_r9's; ColorOS calls their initializers unguarded, One UI 8 has neither), 2026-11-26. r3: ColorOS 17's own telephonycore and webapp modules (One UI 8 has neither; TelephonyServicesInitializer, WebAppFrameworkInitializer). r4: services_patched.jar with the a16_connectivity_compat NetworkTemplate.Builder fallback fixed (register clash in StatsPullAtomService). r5: services_patched.jar also guards the two NetworkStatsManager queries ColorOS makes in StatsPullAtomService itself. r6: useNetstatsPerQueryFlags read as false in services (Wi-Fi poll loop). r7: the empty ConnectivityCallListenerService (calls).
#  app/build.gradle.kts packs exactly these files into the APK and fails the build when out/overlays_x9u_in_1105_a16_r7 differs.
